{"n":"Methicillin Resistance","m":"RES","cx":"UTI","w":"A molecular test that looks for the mecA gene, which makes staphylococci resistant to methicillin and related antibiotics (MRSA).","y":"Finding this resistance gene changes which antibiotics will work and may mean extra infection-control steps.","s":"Detection of mecA means staphylococci in the sample are resistant to flucloxacillin and similar antibiotics.","gl":"Not detected means no mecA resistance gene was found.","gh":"Detected means methicillin-resistant bacteria are present, so different antibiotics are needed.","rr":{"both":{"normal":["Not detected","Negative","No methicillin resistance gene was found."],"high":["Detected","Positive","A methicillin resistance gene was found."]}},"c":["MRSA infection","Urinary tract infection"],"sy":["mecA","MRSA gene"],"t":["Resistance genes are reported with the organism found, so results are read together."],"z":["Staphylococcus aureus","Urine culture"]},
{"n":"Trimethoprim Resistance","m":"RES","cx":"UTI","w":"A molecular test that looks for genes that make bacteria resistant to trimethoprim, a common antibiotic for urine infections.","y":"If resistance is found, trimethoprim is unlikely to work, so a different antibiotic is chosen.","s":"Trimethoprim resistance genes predict treatment failure with trimethoprim.","gl":"Not detected means no trimethoprim resistance genes were found.","gh":"Detected means bacteria in the sample carry trimethoprim resistance, so another antibiotic is needed.","rr":{"both":{"normal":["Not detected","Negative","No trimethoprim resistance genes were found."],"high":["Detected","Positive","Trimethoprim resistance genes were found."]}},"c":["Urinary tract infection"],"sy":["dfrA genes","Trimethoprim resistance genes"],"t":["Trimethoprim resistance is common in E. coli urine infections in the UK."],"z":["Escherichia coli","Urine culture"]},
{"n":"Vancomycin Resistance","m":"RES","cx":"UTI","w":"A molecular test that looks for the vanA and vanB genes, which make enterococci resistant to vancomycin (VRE).","y":"Finding vancomycin resistance changes which antibiotics will work and may need infection-control precautions.","s":"Detection of vanA or vanB means enterococci in the sample are resistant to vancomycin.","gl":"Not detected means no vancomycin resistance genes were found.","gh":"Detected means vancomycin-resistant enterococci are present, so specialist antibiotic choices are needed.","rr":{"both":{"normal":["Not detected","Negative","No vancomycin resistance genes were found."],"high":["Detected","Positive","Vancomycin resistance genes were found."]}},"c":["Vancomycin-resistant enterococcus (VRE) infection"],"sy":["vanA/vanB","VRE genes"],"t":["VRE is usually linked with hospital care and recent antibiotics."],"z":["Enterococcus faecium","Enterococcus faecalis"]},
{"n":"Urine culture","m":"CUL","cx":"UTI","O":"bacteria","w":"A laboratory culture of a urine sample to grow and count bacteria and test which antibiotics will treat them.","y":"It confirms a urinary tract infection and identifies the right antibiotic, especially when infections keep coming back.","s":"Significant growth of one organism confirms a urinary infection when you have symptoms. Mixed growth usually means contamination.","c":["Urinary tract infection","Kidney infection (pyelonephritis)","Asymptomatic bacteriuria"],"sy":["MSU culture","Urine culture and sensitivity","Urine C&S"],"t":["A midstream urine sample reduces contamination. Mixed growth usually means the sample was contaminated."],"z":["Urinalysis (Urine Examination)","Urine pH"]}
